{"availability":"available","full":"HexmosTech/LiveReview","name":"LiveReview","description":"Blast-Radius Aware AI Code Review for Business-Critical Systems","category":"Business","language":"Go","stars":63,"forks":10,"created":"2025-08-26T09:04:00Z","updated":"2026-10-03T15:31:21Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"https://hexmos.com/livereview/","topics":["code","code-analysis","code-quality","code-review","code-reviews"],"demo":"https://hexmos.com/livereview/demo/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T19:21:56.293Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T19:21:56.293Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T19:21:56.293Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:19:16.040Z","stars":63,"forks":10},{"at":"2026-10-04T19:21:56.293Z","stars":63,"forks":10}],"technologies":["Go"],"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T21:19:16.040Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["LiveReview is an AI code reviewer that scores every hunk of a diff by blast radius: how far a change reaches through your call graph, how much persistent state it touches, and how well-tested it is. A 3-line change to a shared auth check can outrank a 300-line UI tweak. Your team's attention goes to the highest-risk code first, not spread evenly across every diff.","LiveReview's Blast Radius & Review Priority scoring, live in the diff viewer.","How does Blast Radius scoring work? (a more technical explanation)"],"features":["A 3-line fix in a function used by 40 other files, that also writes to a database, should score high.","A 300-line UI change in one file, fully covered by tests and used by nothing else, should score low, even though it's the bigger diff.","Blast Radius: how far a change can reach through your code.","How many other places call this code, directly or a few steps removed","Whether it writes to a database or other long-term storage"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HexmosTech/LiveReview/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"5f0b29513e5dc987b192637b235786e9002996cf70a